calendar_read (audit-fail-calendar-read, still firing 2026-10-13):
a dead/mis-shared calendar id in the registry (the literal
\${GOOGLE_CALENDAR_JARVIS_CALENDAR_NAME} script-bug calendar, 404 on
every GET) raised CalendarError inside GoogleCalendar.list_events and
sank the whole aggregate read — every agenda prefetch and calendar_read
failed. Now a per-calendar miss collects into provider.errors which
CalendarService folds into the result's errors[] (degrade, don't fail);
only an all-calendars failure still raises, and CalendarAuthError stays
loud mid-fan-out.

chat_send / /api/notify lane ('deferred notify send failed: NoneType'):
notify_or_defer queued a context note on a provider with no live Gemini
session (ws registered, connect never ran or already closed); the drain
then crashed on _session.send_client_content. notify_or_defer and
_send_context_note now raise RuntimeError('provider is not connected')
like every other send path — /api/notify already retries that exact
error for the connecting window, then reports delivered:false.

Tests: 3 google-adapter cases (partial 404 degrade, all-dead raise,
mid-fan-out 401 stays loud), 2 service cases (intra-provider errors
surface on hit and empty days), 1 provider test (notify_or_defer +
_send_context_note raise unconnected). 76 calendar/provider tests pass,
207 tool_runner tests pass (ADA_INSTANCE_ID=tony; unset run shows only
the pre-existing env-dependent CalendarGate failure).

